Defects found:

1. Line 48: probe keyed to string a fix removes.
Exact input:
```html
<script>_outcomeAvailabilityCount("default"); const seed=["default"]; const labels={default:"CV Death or Worsening HF"};</script>
```
Consequence: after the seed has already been fixed, the remaining bad CV label is unreachable because `SEED not in html` returns `"not-target"`.

2. Line 43: selector keyed to one object layout.
Exact input:
```html
<script>_outcomeAvailabilityCount("x"); const seed=["default","ACM","CVD","ACH","RENAL","RecurrentHF"]; const realData=[{title:"CV death",shortLabel:"CVD"}]; const labels={default:"CV Death or Worsening HF"};</script>
```
Consequence: this CV app is misclassified as non-CV because the regex only matches `{shortLabel:"...",title:"`, so CV labels are wrongly genericized.

3. Lines 81 and 89: CRLF vs LF text handling.
Exact input: a target file containing CRLFs, e.g.
```text
<script>\r\n_outcomeAvailabilityCount("x");\r\n["default","ACM","CVD","ACH","RENAL","RecurrentHF"];\r\n</script>\r\n
```
Consequence: reading normalizes newlines and writing with `newline=""` emits LF, so the whole file can appear changed beyond the intended replacement.

4. Lines 71-74 and 90: status/check can become vacuous.
Exact input: run with any target HTML, but with `jscheck` absent or raising during import.
Consequence: the advertised jscheck gate is silently disabled and the script still prints `APPLIED fixed=1 reverted=0`.

None found in this packet for: merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation, zero conflated with absent, negation dropped.

COULD NOT DETERMINE: whether line 90 reverses pass/fail semantics for `jscheck.check(f)` because `jscheck` is missing from the packet.
